  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Scattered showers and thunderstorms Sunday and \nSunday night. Isolated showers and thunderstorms are possible Monday.\n\nHigh pressure currently over the region will slide east tonight. \nSurface low is forecast to track from the upper Great Lakes Sunday \nto southern New England by Sunday night. This low track will bring a \nsurface warm frontal segment northeast Sunday through Sunday \nevening, sending warmer and more humid air into the region, and be \nfollowed by the passage of a cold front Sunday night and Monday \nmorning.\n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms are expected to develop mainly in \nthe afternoon and evening along and ahead of the surface warm and \ncold fronts as diurnal destabilization develops within the warm\nsector. Severe thunderstorm potential looks limited with only \nmarginal instability and unfavorable shear profiles. PWATs \nrising to near 2.00\" will bring the potential for locally heavy \nrain, but this threat should remain isolated. \n\nKey Message 2...Cold front brings another round of scattered showers \nand possible thunderstorms during the midweek period. \n\nHigh pressure across the region Tuesday will exit by midweek, \nallowing a cold front to move through the region. Current guidance \nbrings the front through late Wednesday and Wednesday night bringing \nanother round of showers and possible thunderstorms.",
